   102	### Technical risks
   103	The leftover processes are found by the `POSE_SEALED_CHECKOUT=<checkout>` entry of their environment, which every process of the run inherits; a process that clears its environment escapes, and the existing cleanup inventory still fails that run (L1). Reading another process's environment needs Linux and the same user; elsewhere the group kill stays the only termination (L2).
